<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krishna Mandir (Patan)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1637</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> Mandir is a stone temple on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-durbar-square">Patan Durbar Square</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitpur-nepal">Lalitpur, Nepal</a>, completed in 1637 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddhi-narasimha-malla">Siddhi Narasimha Malla</a>. Built in the shikhara style of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> rather than the tiered Newar style, it has carved friezes of scenes from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a>. It is one of the finest monuments of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krishna-mandir-patan.jpg" alt="Krishna Mandir (Patan)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chainwit. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lalitpur_Patan_Durbar_Square_2023_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
